Implemented the KOB─░ workflow in `views/kobi.py`, `repo_kobi.py`, and the owned KOB─░ styles in `ui.py`: validated uploads with SHA-256, editable invoice fields, risk checks, financing status transitions, offer comparison and acceptance/rejection, mock transfers, notifications, and audit logging. First uploads of all six live-demo invoices avoid false duplicate flags; repeat invoice fingerprints are still rejected, and offers remain manual.

**Validation:** Python compilation, SQLite workflow checks, and Streamlit AppTest for all three KOB─░ pages passed. The requested Streamlit server responded on port 8512 and was stopped. Commit: `d75e1f7` (clean worktree; not pushed). One limitation: PDF files are accepted and recorded, but this appÔÇÖs local Gemma helper processes images only and no PDF renderer is available, so convert a PDF page to PNG/JPG before extraction. The unread badge is shown within the KOB─░ view rather than the shared top bar, which is outside my file ownership.

### ­şîÉ Community Wisdom
Evidence was limited to two directly relevant articles; the inspected comment threads were empty. ­şøí´©Å [Handling File Uploads in Web Apps: Best Practices Every Developer Should Know](https://dev.to/aaliantaqi/handling-file-uploads-in-web-apps-best-practices-every-developer-should-know-39pa) by [@aaliantaqi](https://dev.to/aaliantaqi) emphasizes validating file contents and size, reflected in the upload checks. ­şöù [Read Full Discussion on DEV](https://dev.to/aaliantaqi/handling-file-uploads-in-web-apps-best-practices-every-developer-should-know-39pa)  
­şöı [Audit Trails for AI Document Workflows: What To Store](https://dev.to/iterationlayer/audit-trails-for-ai-document-workflows-what-to-store-2f4) by [@iterationlayer](https://dev.to/iterationlayer) recommends durable workflow records over scattered logs, consistent with keeping invoice transitions and actions in SQLite. ­şöù [Read Full Discussion on DEV](https://dev.to/iterationlayer/audit-trails-for-ai-document-workflows-what-to-store-2f4)

